    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 150503\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n1003 PM PDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Breezy south-southwesterly wind gusts will continue through the\n  week with dry conditions and near-normal temperatures.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Persistent troughing across the Western US will keep\nthe region in a generally dry and breezy pattern through much of\nthe upcoming week. In the near term, a trough will eject into the\nNorthern Plains today before additional troughing drops south\nalong the Pacific Northwest Coast by midweek. This will keep the\nMojave Desert and southern Great Basin region in a southwesterly\nflow aloft, favoring breezy conditions in the afternoons and any\nlingering monsoonal moisture focused more across central and\neastern Arizona. A few isolated thunderstorms may develop across\neastern Mohave County through midweek, but coverage is expected \nto be quite limited. \n\nOtherwise, thanks to the pattern at hand, temperatures will remain\nnear seasonal normals through the period. The flow pattern will\ntrend more zonal by the weekend allowing for the gusty winds to\nease while temperatures remain near normal. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 06Z Forecast Package...Light \nsouthwest winds tonight give way to breezy south-southeast winds \nTuesday morning and afternoon. Some uncertainty exists in the exact \nwind direction and magnitude during the morning hours (15z-19z). \nThink on average, winds during this time will be from ~160, but \nwouldn't be surprised to see periods as far east as 120. By mid-\nafternoon, expecting a gradual turn to a more true south direction. \nGusts 15-25 knots likely (90%), with 30+ knots possible (25%). Winds \nshould subside after sunset and remain from the south-southwest \novernight. Mostly clear skies with just a few mid-level afternoon \nclouds. Temps peak just shy of 100F on Tuesday.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 06Z Forecast Package...Breezy south winds \nlinger tonight in areas southeast of I-15, but elsewhere light winds \nare expected. Southerly to southeasterly winds pick up across most \nof the region Tuesday morning and persist through sunset. Peak gusts \nof 15-30 knots are likely (90%). Isolated convection possible (10-\n20%) across northwestern Arizona and eastern Lincoln County Tuesday \nafternoon/evening. Here, few to scattered clouds around 10kft are \nexpected, but mostly clear skies farther west.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Outler \nAVIATION...Woods\n\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
